181:/// The action a permission value applies, or the reason it does not resolve.
183:/// opencode accepts two shapes for a permission value: a bare action
184:/// (`"deny"`), and an object of pattern → action (`{"**": "deny"}`). The
185:/// object form is the same rule as the bare one when every pattern in it
186:/// carries the same action, and it is the only form opencode's schema allows
187:/// for `read`, `edit`, `glob`, `grep`, `list`, `bash`, `task`,
188:/// `external_directory`, `lsp` and `skill`. A mixed object is not one action —
189:/// it denies some patterns and allows others — so it is rejected here rather
190:/// than read as whichever action happened to come first.
